  "id": "COMPOUND:18385 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 2-(Methyldithio)Pyridine-N-Oxide may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of target-mediated pathways. This compound is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including 6-O-Veratroylcatalpol and 5,6,8-Trimethoxy-2-Propylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which in turn target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The consistent presence of the compound as a target of CD276 antigen, which is itself a target of these other molecules, indicates a potential mechanism of action involving the CD276 antigen as a bridge between the compound and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The scores assigned to these relationships suggest a moderate level of confidence in the proposed interactions, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a possible role for 2-(Methyldithio)Pyridine-N-Oxide in modulating the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the mechanism.",
